        "filled_by": "remotion:CmpRepeat",
        "at": "2026-11-20T15:59:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "The second trick is like Morse code. The letter E is common, so it gets one dot. Q is rare, so it gets four signals. Common things get short codes, and rare things get long ones.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "speed": 0.95,
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CmpMorse",
          "props": {
            "eAt": 0.1824,
            "qAt": 0.4304,
            "ruleAt": 0.6848,
            "introAt": 0.0496,
            "durationSeconds": 12.5
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.1,
      "render_duration_s": 12.125,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-11-20T15:59:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
      "narration_text": "Here it is for real. I compressed four verses of the rhyme, and four hundred twenty-four bytes became eighty-seven, about a fifth. Unzipped, it was identical. Then I tried random bytes. They got bigger, because there was nothing to repeat.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "speed": 0.95,
      "estimated_duration_s": 20,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CmpLossless",
          "props": {
            "rhymeBytes": 424,
            "rhymeZip": 87,
            "randomBytes": 424,
            "randomZip": 435,
            "identical": true,
            "rhymeAt": 0.1188,
            "zipAt": 0.3348,
            "sameAt": 0.5278,
            "randomAt": 0.7054,
            "biggerAt": 0.8077,
            "footnote": "Real result: demo/compress_demo.py (Python zlib, the DEFLATE method inside ZIP and PNG).",
            "durationSeconds": 15.65
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 15.25,
      "render_duration_s": 15.25,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-11-20T15:59:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "SURPRISE",
      "narration_text": "That's not a bug. There are more long files than short ones, so no compressor can shrink every file. It only wins when there's a pattern.",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "speed": 0.95,
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "source": "own",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "CmpCounting",
          "props": {
            "longAt": 0.1582,
            "ruleAt": 0.4308,
            "patternAt": 0.7407,
            "source": "RFC 1951 (DEFLATE): “no lossless compression algorithm can compress every possible input”",
            "durationSeconds": 9.1
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.7,
      "render_duration_s": 8.708333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
